  "afd": {
    "available": true,
    "issued_at": "2026-10-23T04:59:00+00:00",
    "product_id": "936d0722-3b7a-4d14-8f12-3742dd2927ec",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 230459\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n959 PM PDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Scattered showers and thunderstorms with brief heavy rain, small\n  hail, and lightning will remain possible through this evening.\n  \n* Drier conditions and seasonable temperatures expected this \n  weekend and early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through next Thursday.\n\nA large 564dm low continues to slowly meander across central\nCalifornia this afternoon, with a strong and deep southerly flow\nout ahead of it. This flow pattern has entrained some deeper\nsurface moisture north into the region over the past couple days,\nand as the low moves inland today, cooler air aloft is moving in\nhelping to add to the instability present. This is sparking a few\ncorridors of strong thunderstorm activity again this afternoon.\nDeep layer shear of 40-50 knots or greater is resulting in very\nfast northward storm motions which is helping to limit the flood\nthreat, but enhancing the risk of small to potentially quarter\nsized hail. This risk will remain present through the evening\nhours before instability begins to wane and the corridor of\ninstability and wind shear shifts eastward. \n\nBy tomorrow, the low will have moved inland and begun to weaken\nconsiderably, but weak troughing will remain over head with\nlingering terrain driven showers possible. Conditions will\ncontinue to dry through the weekend and next week with\ntemperatures returning to near normal. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast \nPackage...Showers have exited the area and are not expected through \nthe TAF period. South winds at 10-15KT are expected through 09Z. \nIsolated gusts over 20KT are possible but should be infrequent. \nBetween 09Z-12Z, winds will drop under 8KT, becoming light and \nvariable for the rest of the night into Friday morning. Winds on \nFriday afternoon will remain under 8KT, becoming east in the \nafternoon before backing to the northwest around sunset. A stronger \npush of northwest winds is possible around 09Z Friday night with \nwinds over 10KT and gusts to around 20KT expected. VFR skies will \npersist.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Scattered showers with \nisolated thunderstorms will persist for a few more hours, mainly in \nLincoln County into northwest Arizona. By Friday, other than a few \nshowers in the terrain of Inyo County in the afternoon, it will be \ndry across the region the rest of the TAF period. South to southwest \nwinds at 10-15KT will continue a few more hours before dropping to \nunder 10KT areawide by Friday morning. Winds will generally remain \nat or below 10KT through Friday afternoon, favoring the north to \nnortheast in the afternoon. A front will push through northern Inyo \nCounty and portions of the Southern Great Basin Friday evening, with \nnorthwest winds at 10-15KT and gusts to 25KT expected behind this \nfeature. \n\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Outler\nAVIATION...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
